{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>He gathers</b> — Now he mentioned earth first, for it is the substrate and we are born from it; afterward the heavens, and afterward the sea. He did not mention the sphere of fire and wind, for he spoke only of what is visible to the eye. Rabbi Moses said: the surface of the earth, which is the dry land, is revealed only by the pillar of water, like a heap, for the waters were gathered, and behold כונס is from the same root as לך כנוס את כל היהודים (Esther 4:16), and the meaning of נותן באוצרות is doubled."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The final phrase 'ונותן באוצרות הטען כפול' is textually difficult; read hyper-literally as 'and the meaning given in treasuries is doubled.' It is unclear whether this refers to a doubled sense of אוצרות in the verse or to some other hermeneutical doubling."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:20.552757400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}